==============================================================================
A. d = 2, exact: all 2-planes L in R^4 with omega|_L = 0 and eta|_L = 0
   (six Plucker charts: pivots P, L = {v : v_P free, v_{P^c} = M v_P})
  chart pivots ['x1', 'x2']: equations [b - c, 2*a, b + c, 2*dd]
     solution {a: 0, b: 0, c: 0, dd: 0}  free parameters: []  -> dimension 0
  chart pivots ['x1', 'p1']: equations [a*dd - b*c + 1, 2*a*c, a*dd + b*c + 1, 2*b*dd]
     solution {a: -1/dd, b: 0, c: 0}  free parameters: [dd]  -> dimension 1
  chart pivots ['x1', 'p2']: equations [a + dd, 2*c, a + dd, 2*b]
     solution {a: -dd, b: 0, c: 0}  free parameters: [dd]  -> dimension 1
  chart pivots ['x2', 'p1']: equations [a + dd, 2*c, a + dd, 2*b]
     solution {a: -dd, b: 0, c: 0}  free parameters: [dd]  -> dimension 1
  chart pivots ['x2', 'p2']: equations [a*dd - b*c + 1, 2*a*c, a*dd + b*c + 1, 2*b*dd]
     solution {a: -1/dd, b: 0, c: 0}  free parameters: [dd]  -> dimension 1
  chart pivots ['p1', 'p2']: equations [-b + c, 2*a, b + c, 2*dd]
     solution {a: 0, b: 0, c: 0, dd: 0}  free parameters: []  -> dimension 0
  => the solution set in Gr(2,4) has components of dimension [0, 1]
  family L(theta) = span{(v,0),(0,v_perp)}, v = (cos t, sin t):
     B^T omega B = [[0, 0], [0, 0]]   B^T eta B = [[0, 0], [0, 0]]
     L(0) basis cols: [[1, 0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0, 1]]  L(pi/2): [[0, 1, 0, 0], [0, 0, -1, 0]]
==============================================================================
B. Zariski tangent dimension of {omega|_L = 0, eta|_L = 0} at each coordinate splitting
   chart: L(M) = col(B0 + C0 M), C0 = basis of the opposite splitting; d^2 unknowns
  d = 2: 2^d = 4 coordinate splittings; k=0: tangent dim [0] (k(d-k) = 0, #splittings 1), k=1: tangent dim [1] (k(d-k) = 1, #splittings 2), k=2: tangent dim [0] (k(d-k) = 0, #splittings 1)
  d = 3: 2^d = 8 coordinate splittings; k=0: tangent dim [0] (k(d-k) = 0, #splittings 1), k=1: tangent dim [2] (k(d-k) = 2, #splittings 3), k=2: tangent dim [2] (k(d-k) = 2, #splittings 3), k=3: tangent dim [0] (k(d-k) = 0, #splittings 1)
  d = 4: 2^d = 16 coordinate splittings; k=0: tangent dim [0] (k(d-k) = 0, #splittings 1), k=1: tangent dim [3] (k(d-k) = 3, #splittings 4), k=2: tangent dim [4] (k(d-k) = 4, #splittings 6), k=3: tangent dim [3] (k(d-k) = 3, #splittings 4), k=4: tangent dim [0] (k(d-k) = 0, #splittings 1)
==============================================================================
C. joint symmetry algebra of (omega, eta) and its orbits through the coordinate splittings
  d = 2: dim of joint algebra = 4 (dim gl(d) = 4); all generators diag(a, -a^T): True
         orbit dimension through x_S + p_(S^c), by k = |S|: k=0: [0], k=1: [1], k=2: [0]
  d = 3: dim of joint algebra = 9 (dim gl(d) = 9); all generators diag(a, -a^T): True
         orbit dimension through x_S + p_(S^c), by k = |S|: k=0: [0], k=1: [2], k=2: [2], k=3: [0]
  d = 4: dim of joint algebra = 16 (dim gl(d) = 16); all generators diag(a, -a^T): True
         orbit dimension through x_S + p_(S^c), by k = |S|: k=0: [0], k=1: [3], k=2: [4], k=3: [3], k=4: [0]
